Babet 2.8.0 roadmap
====================

[x] Lot 1: enrich babet.archive.list() without breaking its historical wrapper.
[x] Preserve archive order and expose bounded ZIP/TAR metadata.
[x] Report exact duplicates and normalized output-path conflicts.
[x] Add configurable raw-name and cumulative-name limits shared by inspection
    and extraction.
[x] Add exhaustive ZIP/TAR/worker tests and rich synchronized FR/EN examples.
[x] Lot 2: add babet.archive.test() for complete integrity and safety checks.
[x] Lot 3: add include/exclude safe-glob selection to archive.extract().
[x] Lot 4: add dry_run extraction simulation with no filesystem mutation.
[x] Study the optional bounded babet.archive.read() API: deliberately deferred
    because extractFile() covers targeted extraction and an in-memory API would
    add another allocation/size contract without being required for 2.8.0.
[x] Perform the final code/tests/docs/PDF/build/release audit.

Deferred ideas retained in notes.md:
- bounded in-memory archive.read() for a future version if a concrete use case
  justifies the additional API and memory contract;
- parent-side PATH resolution followed by execve;
- worker-to-worker channels;
- cooperative cancellation design;
- macOS/BSD portability.
